No, it does not fall into any "sac a unicorn" box, since I made no
reference to unicorns nor sacing.  Furthermore, it doesnt work 
the way that you seem to think.  A table of the alignments
of each type of monster can be found at:
  http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/mon2-343.txt
Now, to figure out how much a monster is worth to your alignment when
you kill it, 
  o if the monster is your quest leader, you lose
    your current alignment plus half the alignment limit
  o if the monster if your nemesis, you gain 1/4 the limit
  o if the monster is a guardian, you lose 1/8 the limit
  o if the monster is a priest, +/- 2 for cross/co-aligned,
    additionally 1/4 the limit if the priest is unaligned
  o if the monster is tame, -15
  o if the monster is peaceful, -5
  o ALWAYS the value of 'malign', where  'malign' is computed as follows 
  (which is computed at monster creation time)
 let the absolute value of the alignment from that table be called "absmal",
 unless the monster is a priest or a minion, in which case it is 5* the
 absolute value of their "shrine alignment" or "minion alignment"
 respectively.
  o if the monster is your quest leader -20
  o if the monster is unaligned, 0 if peaceful, 20 if not
  o if the monster class is "always peaceful", and this monster
    was created peaceful -3*max(5,absmal)
  o if the monster class is "always peaceful", and this monster
    was not created peaceful (i.e. renegade) 3*max(5,absmal)
  o if always hostile and colaigned, 0
  o if always hostile but not coaligned max(5,absmal)
  o if coaligned and peaceful, -3*max(3,absmal)
  o if coaligned and not peacful, 3*max(3,absmal)
  o absmal otherwise

So, if you just go kill hostile monsters, your alignment will strictly
increase.
